  "content": "This is the authoritative legend for contact reason categorization at Nathan James. Use this to identify the correct Interaction Type and Interaction Subject for any customer conversation.\n\nPRODUCT ISSUES\n- Defective: All parts intact but product cannot be correctly assembled due to improper manufacturing. Examples: pre-drilled holes wrong size/misaligned, parts bent/warped, improperly welded.\n- Unstable: Product assembles fully but is not sturdy when tightened correctly. Not defective, not broken. Examples: off-balance, wiggles, shaky.\n- Broken Parts: Product cannot be assembled OR is not safe to use because a part is broken/severely damaged. Examples: broken doors, shelves, legs, frame. Significant wood splinters posing safety risk.\n- Damaged in Transit: Box significantly damaged which appears to have caused product damage or missing parts. Examples: customer says box looked destroyed, large hole in box, box arrived soaking wet.\n- Finishing > Surface Imperfections: Product assembles and functions but has a surface defect. Examples: scratches, chips, gouges, discoloration, peeling finish, bubbling laminate, cushion damage.\n- Finishing > Bubbling/Fraying Rattan or Textilene: Rattan or textilene is lifting, bubbling, or fraying (even if considered normal/expected).\n- Finishing > Color Mismatch Between Units: Aesthetic color inconsistency between multiple units or parts of the same SKU.\n- Missing / Wrong / Broken Hardware: Cannot assemble due to missing, wrong, or broken hardware \u2014 resolvable by sending replacement hardware pack.\n- Missing Part: Cannot fully assemble because a part (including inserts) is missing. Product is NOT defective.\n- Wrong Part: Received all parts but they are incorrect; cannot assemble. Example: received 2x Part A instead of 1x Part A and 1x Part B.\n- Missing Instructions: Physical instructions not included in box. NOTE: Customer losing instructions = Product Question, not this.\n\nORDER ISSUES\n- Rec. Duplicate: Customer received too many of the same product.\n- Rec. Wrong Item: Wrong product was shipped \u2014 different from what was ordered.\n- Did Not Receive: Tracking shows delivered but customer says they never received it. Also when tracking was never generated.\n- Lost in Transit: Customer never received item and tracking does not show delivery. Or tracking generated but no movement after 14 days.\n\nNON-GUARANTEE ISSUES (no metadata value \u2014 do not use contactReasonTree for these)\n- Normal Wear and Tear, Damaged During Assembly, Lost Hardware, Damage from Cleaning/Misuse/Modification\n\nORDER MODIFICATIONS\n- Address Change: Wrong address at checkout, updated before shipment left warehouse.\n- In Trans Address Change: Wrong address, updated with carrier while in transit.\n- Return to Sender: Customer cancelled after order shipped; FedEx returning to sender.\n- Item Removal: Item removed from order before shipment.\n- Order Verification: Order flagged by Shopify for Medium or High Risk.\n\nSALES ISSUES\n- Advertising/PDP Error: NJ made an explicit error on PDPs or advertising materials.\n- OOS: Unable to fulfill because item is out of stock.\n- Match Shopify Price (Pre-Purchase): Shopify customer requests price match before purchasing.\n- Match Retailer Price (Pre-Purchase): Customer requests price match vs. another retailer before purchasing.\n- Adjust to Shopify Price (Post-Purchase): Customer requests price adjustment after purchasing on Shopify.\n- Adjust to Retailer Price (Post-Purchase): Customer requests adjustment because retailer now has it cheaper.\n- Content/Expectations: Customer experience does not match product details page.\n\nWAIVED PHYSICAL RETURN\n- Buyer Remorse: Customer returns for reasons outside NJ control, or refund without return for reasons outside NJ control. NOT coordinated through Return Center. Examples: changed mind, doesn't fit space, ordered wrong variant.\n\nCANCELLATION REQUEST\n- Cancelled Order: Customer asks to cancel order. Also applies if order already shipped (pair with RTS or Physical Return).\n\nFEEDBACK\n- Assembly Trouble: Customer struggled to assemble but did NOT damage the item.\n- Persistent Odor/Smell: Item has persistent smell after 1-2 weeks.\n- General Feedback: Positive or negative feedback with no clear product/order/sales issue.\n- Product Requests/Suggestions: Customer shares a suggestion about existing or non-existing product.\n- Sensitive Issue: Sensitive situation requiring special handling.\n\nQUESTIONS\n- Product Question: Customer asks about a specific product or group of products.\n- (No SKU) Materials/Certifications Question: Product questions not related to specific SKUs.\n- Payment/Coupon Question: Customer asks about payment, order, or discount.\n- Where's My Stuff - Non-Backorder Update: Status update on a non-backordered order.\n- Where's My Stuff - Separated Shipments: Status update on remainder of order after some items delivered.\n- Where's My Stuff - Zone-Skip Confusion: Status update on order in Label Created status en route to Kentucky hub.\n- Return Question - Initiate/General Policy: Customer asks about return policy or how to initiate a return.\n- Return Question - Need More Labels: Customer needs more return labels.\n- Return Question - Refund Not Processed Automatically: Return delivered but refund not auto-processed.\n- Return Question - Schedule or Reschedule Pickup: Customer wants to change pickup vs drop-off, or reschedule pickup.\n- Return Question - Change Refund Method: Customer wants to change refund method on a ParcelLab return.\n- Shipping/Assembly Options: Customer asks about shipping/hold options or where we ship.\n- Product Availability: Customer asks when a product will be back in stock.\n- Warranty Registration/General Warranty Info: Customer wants to register for Lifetime Warranty or has general warranty questions. NOTE: Warranty CLAIMS = Product Issues (Defective, Unstable, Finishing, etc.).\n- Trade Account/Designer Discount: Customer inquires about wholesale or trade account.\n- Bulk Order: Customer interested in placing a bulk order.\n- Tax Exempt Inquiry: Customer seeks info on tax-exempt account or tax refund.\n\nOTHER\n- Incomplete Info: Customer reached out by chat, didn't supply contact info, didn't respond, AND chat AI could not resolve all concerns.\n- Missed Callback: We called back after missed call but customer didn't pick up. Only used if no recent conversation to merge into."
